        "content": "## Demonstrator notes \u2014 how traffic-control policies show up in these observability panels\n\nAll data here comes from **passive observation**: `mcp.js` parses MCP JSON-RPC/SSE traffic inside NGINX and nginx-otel exports span attributes \u2014 no client or server changes. Purple vertical markers are policy transitions from the traffic-control plane (hover for what changed; companion dashboard: **MCP traffic control**).\n\n- **open** \u2014 natural shape of the traffic: red+purple on mcp-stable, green on mcp-flaky (its tool error rate ~25% shows in *Error rate per server/client*), blue on mcp-sluggish (`query_db` and `resize_image` dominate *P99 per tool*).\n- **protect-upstreams** \u2014 *RPS per server* for mcp-flaky drops as its dynamic limit clamps; green's RPS falls with it (429s are rejected before reaching the upstream, so error-rate panels here stay unchanged \u2014 rejects are visible on the traffic-control dashboard).\n- **fair-clients** \u2014 *RPS per client* flattens for client-purple at the fair-share cap; other clients unchanged.\n- **full-control** \u2014 the flagship view: in *RPS per server* and *Error rate per client*, client-green's traffic **migrates from mcp-flaky to mcp-stable** as new sessions are rerouted, and green's observed error rate collapses \u2014 same clients, same servers, healthier system.",
